  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (basis cash); proprietary funds on accrual (business_type measure net position, pp14-15). Governmental lines from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (pp8-11); beginning/ending cash are the governmental fund balances 501,970 / 572,634 (p11) that the statement rolls forward (governmental cash 566,222 + 13,912 = 580,134, p7, less 7,500 due to other funds). Total column transfers in 114,000, out 0 (541 interfund eliminated in the Adjustments column); the 114,000 comes from the Electric Fund. Grant Loan Advances/Repayments (community development revolving loans) in other_financing. Proprietary cash-flow statement (pp16-17) not recorded (proprietary is GAAP-only). Balance sheet: the government-wide Statement of Net Position (pp1-2, Total column), since it includes capital assets, loans and debt not on the governmental funds balance sheet. Detail: Schedule of Expenditures by fund (pp20-21; Keno Fund all zero); the total-primary-government budget schedule (pp18-19) combines governmental and business-type revenues and its governmental disbursement lines duplicate the expenditure schedule, so only its four business-type disbursement lines are recorded (no per-fund printed totals for them). Read pages 1-21 of 21"
